    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d239">

                <pb facs="0413" n="1871" sameAs="frus:frus1951v07p2/pg1871"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">293.1111/9–651: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in the Soviet Union
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-12-13T15:15:00-05:00">December 13,
                            1951—3:15 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>410. Urtel 397 Sept 6; Deptel 227 Sept 28 and
                    subsequent Emb approach this subj.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d239-f1"/> Dept desires
                    you see Gromyko, and leave with <pb facs="0414" n="1872" xml:id="pg1872"/> him
                        <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi>, re treatment Amers by Chi Commie
                    auths, stating no reply recd this Govt’s msg delivered Vishinsky by Kirk Sept 4,
                    that one Amer died in prison, one ill in prison died shortly after
                        release<anchor n="2" xml:id="d239-f2"/> and this Govt feels deep anxiety re
                    other Amers in view contd failure obtain satisfactory disposition these
                    long-standing cases. If you perceive objection proposed action inform Dept
                    soonest.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d239-f1" n="1" xml:id="d239-f1-content">
                <p>For telegram 397, September 6, see <ref target="#pg1798">p. 1798</ref>; telegram
                    227, September 28, not printed, instructed Ambassador Kirk that when he called
                    On Vyshinsky prior to his return to the United States, he should again raise the
                    subject of U.S. nationals in China (293.1111/9–651). Kirk reported his
                    conversation with Vyshinsky in telegram 586, October 5, <ref
                        target="frus1951v07p1#pg_1001">p. 1001</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d239-f2" n="2" xml:id="d239-f2-content">
                <p>Philip Cline.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
